{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Repository-local Git configuration can execute a command with factory privileges during either push when an attacker can plant the configuration."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A common local Git identity setting causes the manual landing script to refuse a valid checkout."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The integration tests can exceed the default timeout on a busy or slower machine and fail despite succeeding with a larger budget."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A background process from the checks can change repository configuration after validation and cause the push to execute a command."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A credential embedded in a URL-scoped configuration key is printed unredacted to stderr and captured logs."},{"id":"C1b","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A planted URL rewrite and enabled external transport can execute a command with factory privileges during delivery or landing."}]}